 "response": "Sarun's budget is now **$2,073K**.\n\n**How I applied the policy**\n- I counted only Finance Office records that set or change the budget. Emails, chats, tickets and calls from other teams were ignored.\n- Record #0001 sets the starting point at $1,380K. No later Finance Office record sets an absolute figure, so every later entry is an increase or decrease.\n- Each \"Withdraw update\" record cancels its target, unless that withdrawal is itself withdrawn. I traced each chain from its latest link back to the original update.\n\n**Examples of withdrawal chains**\n- **#0012 does not count.** Chain: #1260 \u2192 #0550 \u2192 #0475 \u2192 #0048 \u2192 #0047 \u2192 #0024 \u2192 #0023 \u2192 #0012. #1260 is active, so #0550 is cancelled and #0475 stands. That cancels #0048, so #0047 stands and cancels #0024. #0023 therefore stands and withdraws #0012.\n- **#0017 counts.** Chain: #0118 \u2192 #0106 \u2192 #0050 \u2192 #0035 \u2192 #0017. #0118 is active, so #0106 is cancelled and #0050 stands. #0050 cancels #0035, so #0017 (\u2212$501K) still applies.\n- **#0020 does not count.** Chain: #1599 \u2192 #0029 \u2192 #0025 \u2192 #0020. #1599 cancels #0029, so #0025 stands and withdraws #0020.\n- **#0517 does not count.** It is withdrawn directly by #1294.\n\n**Result**\nStarting from $1,380K, I applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in record order. The last change counted is #1597 (+$150K), which brings the total to $2,073K.\n\nANSWER: $2073K",
